  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every prime p >= 37 with p congruent to 1 modulo 12, the parameter count N_p defined in problem.md is positive; equivalently, some Alexander quandle Alex(F_p,f_a) in the frozen scope has a nontrivial idempotent in its integral quandle ring. Moreover N_13 = 0, so 13 is the unique prime congruent to 1 modulo 12 without such a parameter.",
